{"blocks":[["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/01%20FCC/","source-block-1156","Ask the dealer or an experienced radio/TV technician for help.",["22.1 FCC","If the unit interferes with radio or television reception, try these measures:"]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/02%20Canada/","source-block-228","22.2 Canada",[]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/02%20Canada/","source-block-244","The Class B digital apparatus complies with Canadian ICES-003.",["22.2 Canada"]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/02%20Canada/","source-block-310","The French statement declares that Class B digital apparatus complies with Canadian standard NMB-003.",["22.2 Canada"]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/03%20CE/","source-block-233","22.3 CE",[]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/03%20CE/","source-block-245","Testing found the unit within the European Council limits for electromagnetic compatibility under Directive 2014/30/EU and low voltage under Directive 2014/35/EU.",["22.3 CE"]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/04%20UKCA/","source-block-229","22.4 UKCA",[]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/04%20UKCA/","source-block-243","The unit meets the essential electromagnetic compatibility requirements of the UK Electromagnetic Compatibility Regulations 2016.",["22.4 UKCA"]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/05%20RoHS/","source-block-231","22.5 ROHS",[]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/05%20RoHS/","source-block-245","The unit uses lead-free solder and meets the requirements of the RoHS Directive 2011/65/EU.",["22.5 ROHS"]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/06%20WEEE/","source-block-169","22.6 WEEE",[]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/06%20WEEE/","source-block-183","The crossed-out wheeled-bin symbol",["22.6 WEEE"]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/06%20WEEE/","source-block-422","This symbol indicates that the electrical and electronic equipment belongs at a collection point for treatment, recovery, and recycling, rather than in household waste. Follow national law and the WEEE Directive 2012/19/EU. For collection information, contact the local municipal office, household waste service, or the shop where the product was purchased.",["22.6 WEEE"]],["Microfreak/UG/22%20Declaration%20of%20Conformity/06%20WEEE/Asset/01-Crossed-out-Wheeled-Bin/png/","source-block-43","01 Crossed-out Wheeled Bin",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/","source-block-132","23 Software License Agreement",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/","source-block-166","Arturia (the Licensor) grants the Licensee a nonexclusive right to use this copy of the software in return for a license fee included in the purchase price. Arturia SA owns all intellectual property rights in the software. Copying, downloading, installing, and using the software are subject to this agreement.",["23 Software License Agreement"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/","source-block-480","Product activation protects against unlawful copying. OEM software requires registration, and activation requires internet access.",["23 Software License Agreement"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/","source-block-614","Installing the software means accepting these terms. If the terms are unacceptable, do not install it. Return the product, including all written material, complete undamaged packaging, and enclosed hardware, to the seller immediately and no later than 30 days after purchase for a refund.",["23 Software License Agreement"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/01%20Software%20Ownership/","source-block-183","1. Software Ownership",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/01%20Software%20Ownership/","source-block-209","Arturia retains full title to the software and every copy, regardless of the media or form in which the original or copies exist. The license does not sell the original software.",["1. Software Ownership"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/02%20Grant%20of%20License/","source-block-266","2. Grant of License",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/02%20Grant%20of%20License/","source-block-290","Arturia grants a nonexclusive license to use the software under this agreement.",["2. Grant of License"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/02%20Grant%20of%20License/","source-block-373","The Licensee may not lease, lend, or sublicense the software. Network use is illegal where the program could be used simultaneously by multiple users.",["2. Grant of License"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/02%20Grant%20of%20License/","source-block-527","The Licensee may make one backup copy for storage purposes only. The Licensee has no rights beyond those specified in the agreement; Arturia reserves all rights not expressly granted.",["2. Grant of License"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/03%20Activation%20of%20Software/","source-block-272","3. Activation of the Software",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/03%20Activation%20of%20Software/","source-block-306","Arturia may require software activation and OEM software registration to control licenses and protect against unlawful copying. The software will not work if the Licensee rejects the agreement.",["3. Activation of the Software"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/03%20Activation%20of%20Software/","source-block-503","In that case, the product, including the software, may be returned only within 30 days of acquisition. A claim under Microfreak/UG/23 Software License Agreement/11 Consequential Damages does not apply upon return.",["3. Activation of the Software"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/04%20Support%2C%20Upgrades%2C%20and%20Updates/","source-block-261","4. Support, Upgrades, and Updates after Product Registration",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/04%20Support%2C%20Upgrades%2C%20and%20Updates/","source-block-326","Support, upgrades, and updates are available only after personal product registration. Support covers the current version and the previous version for one year after a new version is published. Arturia may change the form or extent of support, upgrades, and updates at any time.",["4. Support, Upgrades, and Updates after Product Registration"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/04%20Support%2C%20Upgrades%2C%20and%20Updates/","source-block-608","Registration can occur during activation or later over the internet. It requires agreement to the storage and use of the Licensee’s name, address, contact details, email address, and license data for the purposes described in the agreement. Arturia may share these data with engaged third parties, especially distributors, for support and to verify upgrade or update eligibility.",["4. Support, Upgrades, and Updates after Product Registration"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/05%20No%20Unbundling/","source-block-276","5. No Unbundling",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/05%20No%20Unbundling/","source-block-297","The software is licensed as one product, although the Licensee need not install or use every component. The Licensee may not rearrange components to create a modified version or new product, or modify the software configuration for distribution, assignment, or resale.",["5. No Unbundling"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/06%20Assignment%20of%20Rights/","source-block-259","6. Assignment of Rights",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/06%20Assignment%20of%20Rights/","source-block-287","The Licensee may transfer all software-use rights to another person only if the Licensee transfers this agreement and the software or accompanying hardware, including all copies, upgrades, updates, backup copies, and previous versions that granted upgrade or update rights; retains none of those versions or copies; and the recipient accepts this agreement and the other rules under which the valid license was acquired.",["6. Assignment of Rights"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/06%20Assignment%20of%20Rights/","source-block-711","After the transfer, the product cannot be returned because the recipient rejects the agreement, including its activation requirements.",["6. Assignment of Rights"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/07%20Upgrades%20and%20Updates/","source-block-262","7. Upgrades and Updates",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/07%20Upgrades%20and%20Updates/","source-block-290","Using an upgrade or update requires a valid license for the previous or lower software version. Transferring that version to a third party ends the right to use its upgrade or update.",["7. Upgrades and Updates"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/07%20Upgrades%20and%20Updates/","source-block-477","Acquiring an upgrade or update alone grants no right to use the software. Installing one ends support rights for the previous or lower version.",["7. Upgrades and Updates"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/08%20Limited%20Warranty/","source-block-254","8. Limited Warranty",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/08%20Limited%20Warranty/","source-block-278","Arturia warrants that the supplied software disks are free from defects in materials and workmanship under normal use for 30 days from purchase. The receipt establishes the purchase date. Implied warranties on the software are limited to 30 days, where permitted by state law.",["8. Limited Warranty"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/08%20Limited%20Warranty/","source-block-558","Programs and accompanying materials are provided “as is,” without warranty. The Licensee bears all risk for their quality and performance and all costs of necessary servicing, repair, or correction if a program is defective.",["8. Limited Warranty"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/09%20Remedies/","source-block-261","9. Remedies",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/09%20Remedies/","source-block-277","At Arturia’s option, its entire liability and the Licensee’s exclusive remedy are either a refund of the purchase price or replacement of a disk that fails to meet the limited warranty, returned to Arturia with a copy of the receipt.",["9. Remedies"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/09%20Remedies/","source-block-518","This warranty is void if software failure results from accident, abuse, modification, or misapplication. Replacement software is warranted for the remainder of the original warranty period or 30 days, whichever is longer.",["9. Remedies"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/10%20No%20Other%20Warranties/","source-block-255","10. No Other Warranties",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/10%20No%20Other%20Warranties/","source-block-283","The stated warranties replace all other express or implied warranties, including merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose. Information or advice from Arturia or its dealers, distributors, agents, or employees creates no warranty and does not expand the limited warranty.",["10. No Other Warranties"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/11%20Consequential%20Damages/","source-block-186","11. No Liability for Consequential Damages",[]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/11%20Consequential%20Damages/","source-block-233","Arturia and others involved in creating, producing, or delivering the product are not liable for direct, indirect, consequential, or incidental damages arising from use or inability to use it. Examples include lost business profits, business interruption, and lost business information. This limitation applies even if Arturia was advised that such damages were possible.",["11. No Liability for Consequential Damages"]],["Microfreak/UG/23%20Software%20License%20Agreement/11%20Consequential%20Damages/","source-block-608","State law may prevent limits on implied warranties or exclusions or limits on incidental or consequential damages, so these provisions may not apply. The warranty gives the Licensee specific legal rights, and other rights may vary by state.",["11. No Liability for Consequential Damages"]],["Microfreak/UI/","source-block-63","MicroFreak interface",[]],["Microfreak/UI/","source-block-88","The controls of the Microfreak, by panel position and by section.",["MicroFreak interface"]],["Microfreak/UI/","source-block-161","Areas",["MicroFreak interface"]],["Microfreak/UI/","source-block-173","Microfreak/UI/Front",["MicroFreak interface","Areas"]],["Microfreak/UI/","source-block-201","Microfreak/UI/Rear",["MicroFreak interface","Areas"]],["Microfreak/UI/","source-block-228","Microfreak/UI/Oscillator",["MicroFreak interface","Areas"]],["Microfreak/UI/","source-block-261","Source",["MicroFreak interface"]],["Microfreak/UI/","source-block-274","Microfreak/UG",["MicroFreak interface","Source"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/","source-block-66","Front panel",[]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/","source-block-82","The MicroFreak front panel, in five rows from top to bottom: three rows of controls, the icon strip, and the keys.",["Front panel"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/","source-block-200","Areas",["Front panel"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/","source-block-212","Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/01 Top",["Front panel","Areas"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/","source-block-251","Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/02 Main",["Front panel","Areas"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/","source-block-291","Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03 Bottom",["Front panel","Areas"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/","source-block-333","Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/04 Icon Strip",["Front panel","Areas"]],["Microfreak/U